The comment states "These must be imported at the entry point for Next.js" and "Importing them in the lazy-loaded component doesn't work properly". However, this isn't specific to Next.js - it's actually a Vite library mode bundling issue where CSS imports from node_modules aren't bundled when imported inside lazy-loaded components. The comment should be updated to accurately reflect the technical reason: "Import AG Grid CSS at the entry point because Vite library mode doesn't bundle CSS from node_modules when imported in lazy-loaded components".
```suggestion
// Import AG Grid CSS at the entry point because Vite library mode doesn't bundle
// CSS from node_modules when imported inside lazy-loaded components
```
